# Martian Eye — Autonomous Dust Devil Intelligence

> An end-to-end computer vision and explainable AI (XAI) platform for autonomous detection, multi-object localization, and morphology profiling of Martian dust devil vortices.

---

## Description

**Martian Eye** is a specialized web application and deep-learning pipeline designed for real-time atmospheric surveillance on Mars. The system processes planetary surface imagery (MER Navcam, Sol Pancam) and orbital satellite data (HiRISE) to identify transient dust devil column structures under challenging terrain and atmospheric conditions.

The platform addresses high false-positive rates caused by Martian topography—such as crater rims, dune ripples, and mesa shadows—by combining a primary **Multiscale Spatial Attention Transformer** with a **Stage-2 Hard-Negative Screening Classifier**. The web frontend provides interactive XAI telemetry (Grad-CAM heatmaps), uncertainty estimation, morphology metrics, cross-mission domain adaptation benchmarks, and a 3D perspective HTML5 Canvas background.

---

## Key Features

- **Multiscale Attention Transformer Backbone**: Hybrid ResNet-34 backbone with a 4-head spatial cross-attention block (`MultiscaleSpatialAttention`) for multiscale feature fusion.
- **Multi-Object Plume Detection**: Identifies and bounds single or multiple vertical dust devil plumes per image frame using vertical structure morphological filters (`cv2.MORPH_TOPHAT` / `cv2.MORPH_BLACKHAT`), Sobel vertical gradients, and Non-Maximum Suppression (NMS).
- **Strict Negative Detection Gate**: Evaluates candidate confidence against a configurable threshold slider; non-plume surface frames cleanly return `No dust devil found` with zero false-positive bounding boxes.
- **Candidate-Focused Grad-CAM Heatmaps**: Spatial attention heatmaps (`GradCAMExplainer`) concentrated around candidate regions using a 2D Gaussian focus kernel.
- **Stage-2 Hard-Negative Verifier**: Hard-negative screening model (`HardNegativeFalsePositiveClassifier`) built on MobileNet-V3 Small to screen out topographic landforms.
- **Atmospheric Morphology Analysis**: Calculates candidate width, height, aspect ratio, orientation angle, and estimated physical dimensions (`DustDevilMorphologyAnalyzer`).
- **Dynamic Port & Server Launcher**: Node.js launcher (`server.js`) that spawns a Python Uvicorn backend process with automatic port fallback (`3000`, `3001`, `3002`) and Express reverse proxying.
- **3D Solar System Canvas Engine**: HTML5 Canvas rendering 8 revolving planets along 3D elliptical orbits around a luminous central Sun, with upper spiral galaxy nebulae.

